<!-- The temporal companion to the Key Locations maps: the maps answer
     "where am I?", this page answers "when am I?". Everything below is
     driven by study_slug: the SVG is drawn by _partials/_timeline.erb from
     src/_data/{study}/timeline.yml, and the listing renders the same data
     as linked text, so the content is never locked inside the graphic. A
     future study's timeline page can copy this file and change only the
     front matter (and the prose). -->

<p>
  The maps on the location pages answer the question <em>where am I?</em> This
  page answers its companion: <em>when am I?</em> One century holds the whole
  New Testament -- from a birth in Bethlehem near the end of Herod the Great's
  reign to an old man's visions on Patmos -- and seeing the events in order
  changes how the letters read. Romans sits between the Corinthian letters and
  the arrest at Jerusalem; Revelation stands a full lifetime after Pentecost.
</p>

<p>
  A word of honesty before the chart: almost every date here is approximate.
  Ancient sources rarely hand us a year, so scholars triangulate from rulers'
  reigns, festivals, and the letters' own travel notes. Ranges below are shown
  as ranges on purpose. This chart follows the AD 30 crucifixion date; the
  main alternative, AD 33, would shift the ministry and the church's first
  years about three years later without changing the shape of the story.
</p>

<%= render "timeline", study: data.study_slug %>

<%
  study    = data.study_slug
  study_tl = site.data.send(study.gsub("-", "_")).timeline
  wp       = site.data.send(study.gsub("-", "_")).week_phases

  week_url = ->(wk) do
    sec = wp[wk] || wp[wk.to_s] || wp[wk.to_i]
    relative_url "/#{study}/#{sec}/week-#{format('%02d', wk.to_i)}/overview/"
  end

  entry_li = ->(ev) do
    name  = ev[:name] || ev[:label]
    inner = ev[:slug] ? %(<a href="#{relative_url(ev[:slug])}"><strong>#{name}</strong></a>) : "<strong>#{name}</strong>"
    line  = %(#{inner} <span class="tl-dates">(#{ev[:dates]})</span>)
    line += %( -- #{ev[:note]}) if ev[:note]
    line += %( <a class="tl-week-link" href="#{week_url.(ev[:week])}">Read in Week #{ev[:week]}</a>) if ev[:week]
    line
  end

  render_list = ->(events) do
    items = events.map { |ev| "<li>#{entry_li.(ev)}</li>" }.join("\n")
    %(<ul class="location-index">\n#{items}\n</ul>)
  end
%>

